{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4aefddc6-9763-42f4-a404-7ad9ee57abd2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-984852b2f14e8b8d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-tew96lw_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Configure the OGX pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground RAG\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic wires Gen AI Studio playground RAG to use a remote pgvector-backed vector store, replacing the dependency on the inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the OGX distribution. The gen-ai BFF, which creates OGXServer instances for the playground, is extended to configure the OGX vector_io provider as remote pgvector, consuming PostgreSQL connection details from a secret. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector store implementation can be largely reused — the integration surface is configuration, not new provider code — and this work is independent of who provisions the database (the provider consumes a connection string under every provisioning approach).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation so that a playground with RAG enabled configures the remote pgvector vector_io provider (via the OGX provider-activation mechanism, e.g. `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`), with connection details supplied from a Kubernetes secret.\n- Reuse the existing remote vector store implementation for the pgvector integration.\n- Scope the vector store per playground namespace (per-namespace isolation), matching the Staff Engineer's preferred scoping model.\n- Leave the OGX application storage backend untouched on its existing default — vector storage and application storage are independent configurations; no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope.\n- Ensure the configuration works for disconnected installs (no assumption of external image or dependency fetches beyond what the platform already references).\n- Document guidance for users with production-scale vector workloads on pointing RAG at an external vector database (migration path off the dev-experimentation default).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A playground with RAG configured results in an OGXServer whose vector_io provider is the remote pgvector provider — not an inline provider — running as a separate process from the OGX instance.\n- Vector insert, query, and delete operations through the playground RAG workflow succeed against a pgvector-backed instance with no loss of current capability.\n- The provider consumes PostgreSQL connection details from a secret; no manual provider setup is required from the user beyond the database being reachable.\n- The OGX application storage backend remains on its existing default (no application-storage migration).\n- The vector store is scoped per playground namespace.\n- Documentation describes how users can configure an external, production-grade vector database for RAG workloads that outgrow the default.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 — Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability (delivered by this epic; verified by the benchmark work).\n- AC-4 — the default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (remote provider, not inline).\n- Staff Engineer Corrections 1 and 3 — OGX defaults to SQLite for application storage (PostgreSQL is new work, scoped to the provisioning decision); vector storage configuration is independent of application storage configuration.\n- Staff Engineer directive / open question on migration path — resolved as documented guidance for external vector databases.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65329,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aebb304c45787a7b","agent_id":"abc2c9b5f097a6743","session_id":"aa08