{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-db8ee187-5887-477e-86dc-4b830b17b384","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a17be3209e32938b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-tew96lw_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003.md","content":"# Operator-based self-provisioning of PostgreSQL/pgvector for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n\n## Description\n\nBranch outcome A, executed if the go/no-go decision selects operator-based provisioning — i.e. the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers a RHOAI-controlled operator for Gen AI Studio in time for the target release. This epic implements PostgreSQL lifecycle management in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's pattern of auto-provisioning a PostgreSQL database per managed instance. It uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector included (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`); no custom image build or pipeline onboarding is needed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement per-namespace PostgreSQL self-provisioning for playgrounds with RAG enabled, in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer, following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases.\n- Provision the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) with generated credentials stored in a secret, exposed to the playground's OGXServer as the vector_io provider connection.\n- Seed PostgreSQL resource requests/limits from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing as the starting point.\n- Handle lifecycle via the operator reconciliation loop: cleanup on playground deletion, recovery on pod restarts, credential management.\n- Keep the image reference resolvable for disconnected installs, reusing the platform's existing related-image mechanism for the PostgreSQL 16 image.\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available (following release), consume the shared connection string instead of self-provisioning.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A playground with RAG configured in a namespace has a running, pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance provisioned without any user action beyond enabling the playground.\n- The provisioned database's connection details are available to the OGX vector_io provider via a secret, and playground RAG workflows succeed end to end against it.\n- Lifecycle behaviors are handled by reconciliation: deleting the playground cleans up the provisioned database; pod restarts and credential handling recover without manual intervention.\n- PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator reference sizing, with any adjustments justified.\n- The image reference is overridable for disconnected installs through the platform's existing related-image mechanism.\n- The design documents the migration path to consuming the platform-provided shared database connection string when it becomes available.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 — a default vector store is available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure.\n- AC-4 — the vector store runs as a separate process (a standalone PostgreSQL deployment), decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- AC-5 — scoped for multi-tenant environments via per-namespace isolation.\n- AC-6 — lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments (sizing seeded from the reference operator).\n- Staff Engineer directives: model-registry-operator pattern for self-provisioning; hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 for the operator layer; existing RH PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector; resource sizing reference.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":66905,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aebb304c45787a7b","agent_id":"abc2c9b5f097a6743","session_id":"aa08db75-5b60-4f93-a4ef-03fc