{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beeb76f2423e9b12","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003\n3\ttitle: Operator-based self-provisioning of PostgreSQL/pgvector for Gen AI Studio (branch\n4\t  A)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from the dashboard operator\n17\t    modularization is not delivered in time for the target release, this epic is removed\n18\t    and provisioning moves to the BFF-managed fallback path; as a last resort customers\n19\t    supply their own PostgreSQL by configuring the OGXServer custom resource, which\n20\t    degrades the out-of-the-box experience.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n25\t  existing_foundation: 0\n26\t  open_questions: -1\n27\t  external_dependency: -1\n28\t  human_process_gates: 0\n29\t  repo_access: 0\n30\t  architecture_claims: 1\n31\timplementation_type: null\n32\tinvestigation_signals: null\n33\tai_implementability: Medium\n34\tai_implementability_score: 2\n35\tjira_key: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Operator-based self-provisioning of PostgreSQL/pgvector for Gen AI Studio (branch A)\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tBranch outcome A, executed if the go/no-go decision selects operator-based provisioning — i.e. the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers a RHOAI-controlled operator for Gen AI Studio in time for the target release. This epic implements PostgreSQL lifecycle management in that operator layer, following the model-registry-operator's pattern of auto-provisioning a PostgreSQL database per managed instance. It uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector included (`registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`); no custom image build or pipeline onboarding is needed.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Implement per-namespace PostgreSQL self-provisioning for playgrounds with RAG enabled, in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer, following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases.\n46\t- Provision the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image (pgvector included) with generated credentials stored in a secret, exposed to the playground's OGXServer as the vector_io provider connection.\n47\t- Seed PostgreSQL resource requests/limits from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL sizing as the starting point.\n48\t- Handle lifecycle via the operator reconciliation loop: cleanup on playground deletion, recovery on pod restarts, credential management.\n49\t- Keep the image reference resolvable for disconnected installs, reusing the platform's existing related-image mechanism for the PostgreSQL 16 image.\n50\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available (following release), consume the shared connection string instead of self-provisioning.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A playground with RAG configured in a namespace has a running, pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance provisioned without any user action beyond enabling the playground.\n55\t- The provisioned database's connection details are available to the OGX vector_io provider via a secret, and playground RAG workflows succeed end to end against it.\n56\t- Lifecycle behaviors are handled by reconciliation: deleting the playground cleans up the provisioned database; pod restarts and credential handling recover without manual intervention.\n57\t- PostgreSQL resource requests/limits are set from the model-registry-operator reference sizing, with any adjustments justified.\n58\t- The image reference is overridable for disconnected installs through the platform's existing related-image mechanism.\n59\t- The design documents the migration path to consuming the platform-provided shared database connection string when it becomes available.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- AC-1 — a default vector store is available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning or configuration of external infrastructure.\n64\t- AC-4 — the vector store runs as a separate process (a standalone PostgreSQL deployment), decoupled from the OGX instance.\n65\t- AC-5 — scoped for multi-tenant environments via per-namespace isolation.\n66\t- AC-6 — lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments (sizing seeded from the reference operator).\n67\t- Staff Engineer directives: model-registry-operator pattern for self-provisioning; hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 for the operator layer; existing RH PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector; resource sizing reference.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4690990295981d0","agent_id":"ad43b990017bf9d40","session_id":"aa08db75-5b60-4f93-a4ef-03fcf69423a1","uuid":"bf27cc54-9870-4090-9ee9-73365d96452d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:35:00.183Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-beeb76f2423e9b12","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
