nd the branch epics is justified by Rule 15 (same repo, different areas) and documented. E004 depending only on E002 (not on a branch epic) is the rule-compliant shape — the benchmark can stand up its own pgvector instance, and a main-plan→branch edge would be a critical violation. Critical path length 2 is reasonable for this strategy's size and reflects intended parallelism.\n36\t\n37\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n38\tAll epics use canonical component `Gen AI Studio` (verified against `.context/rhai-components.txt`) and one team (`dashboard-crimson-scrum`), matching the strategy label and the Staff Engineer's framing of Gen AI Studio as the owning feature. The non-obvious component mapping for branch A (work in the operator layer delivered by RHAISTRAT-7164) is logged in the decomposition summary as required. The two branch epics are mutually exclusive conditional alternatives, not scope duplication. E002 (provider wiring) and the branch epics (database provisioning) are complementary producer/consumer surfaces, not duplicated deliverables; the overlap at the connection-secret boundary is incidental. No epic exceeds ~2 weeks: E002 is configuration wiring with a reusable implementation, the branch epics each follow an existing in-platform pattern, E004 is a scoped benchmark. No work-product type mixing — no epic bundles code with sample notebooks/tutorials/content deliverables.\n39\t\n40\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n41\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (go/no-go on the RHAISTRAT-7164 operator layer) determines which branch epic exists — it passes the \"does the outcome change downstream structure\" test, and both branches gate on it. E002, E004, and both branch epics are Implementations producing concrete artifacts (BFF provider configuration, benchmark report + sizing recommendation, provisioning implementations). Signal sets are type-appropriate (Investigation carries `investigation_signals`; Implementations carry `ai_signals`). All `gated_by` fields are set only where an Investigation appears in `dependencies`, every `gated_by` target is in the epic's direct `dependencies` list, and every `gate_failure_impact` has both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated with meaningful content.\n42\t\n43\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n44\tE001's five investigation signals match the rubric conditions: question_specificity +1 (concrete, enumerable question with a defined pass/fail — recorded decision by decision date), source_accessibility 0 (correctly acknowledging the answer is a future delivery outcome plus a team decision, not a readable artifact — the exact case the rubric's 0 covers), local_runnability 0, cluster_hardware_dependence -1 (peripheral verification only), human_judgment_required -2 (the gating question is itself a sprint-planning governance decision — the rubric's -2 case verbatim). Implementation signal values were cross-checked against the 9-signal rubric and the strategy: E002's all-+1 set is justified (named file/mechanism, reusable implementation, no external dependency); E004's 0s on pattern_precedent/adapter_pattern/existing_foundation correctly reflect a greenfield benchmark harness; Branch A's negatives (open_questions -1, external_dependency -1, repo_access 0) correctly reflect building on the undelivered RHAISTRAT-7164 operator layer. architecture_claims +1 rationales cite specific files, and this review independently verified those citations against `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/` — ogx-distribution.md (remote PGVector backend, inline providers stripped), odh-dashboard.md (gen-ai BFF sidecar), model-registry-operator.md (controller-created `{registry-name}-postgres` Deployments), and ogx-k8s-operator.md (upstream-synced operator) all corroborate the claimed premises. No calibration misses. (ai_implementability totals are pipeline-computed and not reviewed, per instructions.)\n45\t\n46\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (0/2)\n47\tACs are present and testable across all five epics, and no epic references sibling epics by draft ID in its body. However, one rule-mandated AC is missing. **E002 is the replacing Implementation epic — its own Description states it wires playground RAG to a remote pgvector store \"replacing the dependency on the inline Milvus provider\" — and Rule 23 requires a rollback/feature-flag AC on the replacing epic. E002 has none.** All six of its ACs assert forward behavior of the new path. A rollback/feature-flag AC is both meaningful and cheap here: the OGX distribution activates providers via environment-variable guards (per ogx-distribution.md), so an AC such as \"the pgvector provider activation is reversible — the BFF can revert a playground to the previous inline-provider default while inline providers still exist in the distribution (i.e., before RHAISTRAT-7474 lands)\" is directly implementable and testable. Per the scoring rule, a missing rule-mandated AC is a major issue and forces this criterion to 0. (No konflux-chain or docs-authoring epics exist, so Rules 24-25 ACs are not applicable; no non-testable externally-controlled ACs were found — E001's sprint-planning ACs are conditions on the epic's own deliverable, the decision record.)\n48\t\n49\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n50\tEvery available strategy element is accounted for: all six acceptance criteria (AC-3 descoped with documented Staff Engineer precedence), all three success criteria (7474 unblocking mapped to E002 + selected branch; no-manual-setup to the branch epics; no-regression to E004's order-of-magnitude benchmark), both open questions, and every Staff Engineer directive (Corrections 1-3, the go/no-go gate, both fallback paths, performance scoping, resource sizing, portability to the 3.6 shared database, remote-vector-store reuse). The conditional branches cover the bounded outcomes: A (operator lands), B (operator slips), and the third outcome — neither self-provisioning path viable, customers bring their own PostgreSQL — is correctly handled as documented gate-failure fallback text rather than an epic, since it requires no engineering deliverable; E001's AC requires it to be documented with user-facing impact. Strategy-level context (release-timing risk, missing attachment, scoping-direction resolution) is carried in Health Warnings rather than silently dropped. No docs-authoring epic is required: the strategy's available sections contain no Prerequisites & Process Gates entry mandating Documentation Support (the validator's Rule 11 check also passes).\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-845053e888497d18","agent_id":"afc2645dc94067da3","session_id":"aa08db75-5b60-4f93-a4ef-03fcf69423a1","uuid":"997e6280-98fc-41b5-b575-dbddef0d9837","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:39:02.103Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aad63c56b092cfa7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
