{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9280d2b29706cbc5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Go/no-go decision: PostgreSQL provisioning approach for the Gen AI Studio\n4\t  default vector store'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Go/no-go decision: PostgreSQL provisioning approach for the Gen AI Studio default vector store\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis epic resolves the central open decision in the strategy: how the default pgvector-backed vector store's PostgreSQL database is provisioned for Gen AI Studio in the current release. Operator-based self-provisioning requires a RHOAI-controlled operator for Gen AI Studio, which the dashboard operator modularization effort (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) is expected to provide; if that does not land in time for the target release, the fallback is BFF-managed provisioning in the gen-ai BFF. The Staff Engineer Input directs the development team to define a go/no-go gate for this decision as part of sprint planning. The outcome selects which provisioning implementation is executed and is recorded as a decision document.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Assess the delivery readiness and timeline of the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) against the target release dates.\n35\t- Define the go/no-go gate criteria and decision date in sprint planning, tied to the release milestone.\n36\t- Evaluate the two viable provisioning approaches against the strategy's requirements:\n37\t  - Out-of-the-box experience: no manual user provisioning or configuration.\n38\t  - Lifecycle management: cleanup on playground deletion, handling of pod restarts, credential rotation (a BFF is not an operator with a reconciliation loop, so these need explicit design attention).\n39\t  - Portability to the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL expected in the following release (consume a shared connection string rather than self-provision).\n40\t  - Per-namespace isolation for multi-tenant scoping.\n41\t- Record the selected approach, the evidence, and the impact of each outcome on the out-of-the-box requirement.\n42\t- Document the last-resort fallback — customers supplying their own PostgreSQL by configuring the OGXServer custom resource — including its user-facing impact, in case neither self-provisioning path is viable.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- A written decision record identifies the selected provisioning approach and cites the evidence used (operator modularization delivery status, lifecycle-management trade-off analysis).\n47\t- Go/no-go gate criteria and a decision date are defined and agreed in sprint planning, anchored to the target release.\n48\t- The decision record documents, for each outcome, the impact on the out-of-the-box experience requirement.\n49\t- The last-resort fallback (customer-supplied PostgreSQL via OGXServer configuration) is documented with its user-facing impact.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- Gates AC-1 (out-of-the-box default vector store) and AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping): the decision determines how per-namespace provisioning is delivered.\n54\t- Staff Engineer directives: hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 for operator-based self-provisioning; go/no-go gate to be defined in sprint planning; fallback paths (BFF-managed provisioning, customer-supplied PostgreSQL).\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a48e6c1126e1b360","agent_id":"a2328aea6b3a75f23","session_id":"aa08db75-5b60-4f93-a4ef-03fcf69423a1","uuid":"5b6b87bf-112b-4ff6-996e-11994ca38c37","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:40:18.802Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9280d2b29706cbc5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004"}
