{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa7b832bc62740c5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Configure the OGX pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground\n4\t  RAG\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: dashboard-crimson-scrum\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 9\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Configure the OGX pgvector vector_io provider for Gen AI Studio playground RAG\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic wires Gen AI Studio playground RAG to use a remote pgvector-backed vector store, replacing the dependency on the inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the OGX distribution. The gen-ai BFF, which creates OGXServer instances for the playground, is extended to configure the OGX vector_io provider as remote pgvector, consuming PostgreSQL connection details from a secret. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector store implementation can be largely reused — the integration surface is configuration, not new provider code — and this work is independent of who provisions the database (the provider consumes a connection string under every provisioning approach).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation so that a playground with RAG enabled configures the remote pgvector vector_io provider (via the OGX provider-activation mechanism, e.g. `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`), with connection details supplied from a Kubernetes secret.\n39\t- Reuse the existing remote vector store implementation for the pgvector integration.\n40\t- Scope the vector store per playground namespace (per-namespace isolation), matching the Staff Engineer's preferred scoping model.\n41\t- Leave the OGX application storage backend untouched on its existing default — vector storage and application storage are independent configurations; no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration is in scope.\n42\t- Ensure the configuration works for disconnected installs (no assumption of external image or dependency fetches beyond what the platform already references).\n43\t- Document guidance for users with production-scale vector workloads on pointing RAG at an external vector database (migration path off the dev-experimentation default).\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- A playground with RAG configured results in an OGXServer whose vector_io provider is the remote pgvector provider — not an inline provider — running as a separate process from the OGX instance.\n48\t- Vector insert, query, and delete operations through the playground RAG workflow succeed against a pgvector-backed instance with no loss of current capability.\n49\t- The provider consumes PostgreSQL connection details from a secret; no manual provider setup is required from the user beyond the database being reachable.\n50\t- The OGX application storage backend remains on its existing default (no application-storage migration).\n51\t- The vector store is scoped per playground namespace.\n52\t- The provider switch is reversible: the BFF can revert a playground to the previous inline-provider default (by disabling the pgvector provider activation, e.g. the `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` guard) while inline providers still exist in the distribution — i.e., before RHAISTRAT-7474 lands — with the playground returning to inline-provider RAG behavior.\n53\t- Documentation describes how users can configure an external, production-grade vector database for RAG workloads that outgrow the default.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- AC-2 — Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store with no loss of current capability (delivered by this epic; verified by the benchmark work).\n58\t- AC-4 — the default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (remote provider, not inline).\n59\t- Staff Engineer Corrections 1 and 3 — OGX defaults to SQLite for application storage (PostgreSQL is new work, scoped to the provisioning decision); vector storage configuration is independent of application storage configuration.\n60\t- Staff Engineer directive / open question on migration path — resolved as documented guidance for external vector databases.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a83b4a1fcd8be7d","agent_id":"a5caa00a7e8404331","session_id":"aa08db75-5b60-4f93-a4ef-03fcf69423a1","uuid":"7557acd8-664a-48fb-8437-a3d9cef8b045","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:45:38.597Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa7b832bc62740c5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Final re-review RHAISTRAT-8004"}
